Add a null check at the beginning of the method to ensure the `sessionId` is not null before attempting to compute the hash.

```java
public boolean validateSession(String sessionId) {
    if (sessionId == null) {
        return false; // Or return false immediately if critical context is needed
    }
    String sessionHash = sessionId.hashCode() + "" + getCurrentTime();
    String hash = getMD5Hash(sessionHash); 
    return hash.equals(expectedHash);
}
```

Using the ternary `?:` operator achieves the same result in less code:

```java
return sessionId == null ? false : ...;
```

